float32-graph-v1 third-party notices
====================================

runtime/src/float32/math.c contains ports of single-precision math routines from musl libc 1.2.5
(https://musl.libc.org, MIT license) and, through musl, from the FreeBSD msun library (Sun Microsystems notice).
Nothing else in runtime/src/float32/ is third-party code.

Where the sources came from
---------------------------
The files were read from the musl 1.2.5 tree that ships inside the Zig 0.14.1 toolchain used to build this
repository (lib/libc/musl/); no code was downloaded for this change.
Canonical upstream locations of the same files (not fetched here):

  musl 1.2.5      https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/tree/src/math/<file>?h=v1.2.5
  FreeBSD msun    https://cgit.freebsd.org/src/tree/lib/msun/src/<s_erff.c | s_expm1f.c | s_tanhf.c>
  Arm optimized   https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines  (math/expf.c, math/exp2f_data.c)

